//
// A PLAIN VARIABLE INDEX STORED UNDISCHARGED IS (N-Store)'S WARNING (`@FR-N-Index`, `@FR-N-Store`).
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard for a rule no test named; every cell answered as the
//   rule says on both backends on the tree it landed on.
// CHANNEL: the expected warning.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the warning names the slot.
// HOLDS: every cell on both backends.
// @EXPECT_WARNING: a nullable `integer?` is stored into the local `x` of the non-null type `integer`

fn main() {
  v = [10, 20];
  i = 1;
  x: integer = v[i];
  assert(x == 20, "the value is right: {x}");
}
